  "adaptations": [
    "Native cancellation-free route options use owned strings and Option request IDs; absent prompt IDs use the same empty-string identity and omitted completion evidence uses Value::Null.",
    "Original JavaScript undefined configuration fields remain absent optional Rust fields. Default serialized configurations are checked by the existing core router-contract corpus.",
    "The advanced clock value in definition5 is retained. The frozen Node schedule actually reads its injected clock zero times because tasks remain active or pending; native boundary clock-read counts differ and are not asserted equivalent.",
    "Native mock implements the typed HTTP transport and returns the unchanged original confidence/tier JSON. No provider network calls, token-count function or classifier verdict stubs are used.",
    "Original internal record/attempt/tool-owner observations use the equivalent core TurnState accessors through the native router policy lock."
  ],
